import{_ as t}from"./chunks/synth_oh3.BkNeNxCu.js";import{_ as a,o as s,c as i,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.hw3Av5Vn.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Oh3","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"synths/engines/OH3.md","filePath":"synths/engines/OH3.md"}'),n={name:"synths/engines/OH3.md"};function h(r,e,d,l,c,f){return s(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="oh3" tabindex="-1">Oh3 <a class="header-anchor" href="#oh3" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Oh3&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Oh3 is the acid bass: one voice of a saw, or the square a transistor shapes from it, through the <a href="./../ENVELOPES#acid-gate">acid gate</a> with its accents, a short sweep into the squelchy <a href="./../FILTERS#diode">diode filter</a> and a pedal&#39;s gentle <a href="./../EFFECTS#drive">drive</a>, sliding from a note into the next where the pattern&#39;s Glide switch carries it, over its circuit&#39;s slide time. A note at the acid gate&#39;s Accent at velocity or louder is accented: its filter opens further and falls fast, it swells for a moment, and a run of accents climbs higher.</p><p><img src="'+t+'" alt="The Oscillators tab of Oh3"></p><h2 id="stock-and-modded" tabindex="-1">Stock and Modded <a class="header-anchor" href="#stock-and-modded" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Stock and Modded&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Acid gate and the Diode filter each have a Circuit, Stock or Modded, after the modifications players made to the original machine, so a Modded envelope can play through a Stock filter. Oh3 slides into a glided note over its Glide time on the Engine tab, 60 ms by default as the original circuit&#39;s fixed slide, and longer for a lazy line.</p><h2 id="how-oh3-is-built" tabindex="-1">How Oh3 Is Built <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-oh3-is-built" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How Oh3 Is Built&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Oh3 follows Open303, an open emulation of the acid bass by Robin Schmidt, whose constants were measured from the circuit; <a href="./../../CREDITS">Credits</a> names it. Its saw is a plain rising ramp in band-limited tables of its own. Its square is made from that saw as the transistor makes it: the saw through a very steep curve, offset so that it switches a little off the middle, then shifted half a cycle and played at half the saw&#39;s level. Because the curve&#39;s edge takes a fixed time, the square sounds like a pulse on low notes and more like a saw on high ones, as the original&#39;s does. The oscillator&#39;s output is turned over and coupled into the filter through a high-pass, as the circuit couples it, which shapes the low end. Tuning shifts the whole voice by semitones, Detune by cents and Fine by tenths of a cent.</p><p>Oh3&#39;s character is in the parts its engine chooses around that oscillator: the acid gate&#39;s accent and its charging capacitor, the Diode filter with a high-pass inside its feedback, so that its resonance sings rather than booms, and its one voice, so that a glided step slides into the next without starting the envelopes again. Any of those can be swapped, and any of them can be given to another engine.</p>',8)])])}const g=a(n,[["render",h]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
